  "worked_solution": "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=\u27e81,0,3\u27e9.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =3i-15j+15k \\\\  & =\u27e83,-15,15\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e83,-15,15\u27e9 & =\u27e81,0,3\u27e9\\cdot \u27e83,-15,15\u27e9 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e83,-15,15\u27e9 & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9\\cdot \u27e83,-15,15\u27e9 & =48 \\\\ 3x-15y+15z & =48 \\\\ 3x-15y+15z-48 & =0 \\\\ x-5y+5z-16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
